# Governance Proposal: Fix pigeon.py f-string syntax error (line 181)

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI)
**Date:** 2026-02-28
**Type:** Bug Fix
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary

`core/pigeon.py` line 181 has an invalid f-string generated by the fleet. The fleet attempted to escape single quotes using `chr(39)` but produced unparseable syntax: `result[chr(39)]category[chr(39)]`. This causes a 500 on every `/api/pigeon/droppings` call because Python cannot import the module.

## Proposed Changes

**File:** `core/pigeon.py`
**Location:** Line 181

## Risk Assessment

- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES
- **Dependencies:** None — server hot-reloads on fix
- **Testing:** `GET /api/pigeon/droppings` should return 200 after restart

## Implementation

```python
path = r"C:/Users/Sean/Documents/GitHub/Willow/core/pigeon.py"
with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
    content = f.read()

old = "logger.info(f\"PIGEON: filed {item.name} -> {result[chr(39)]category[chr(39)]}/\")"
new = "logger.info(f\"PIGEON: filed {item.name} -> {result['category']}/\")"

assert old in content, f"Pattern not found — file may have changed. Snippet around line 181: {content[4800:5100]}"
content = content.replace(old, new, 1)

with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
    f.write(content)

print("Applied: fix-pigeon-fstring-001")
```

